\title{Grazing Snails and Algal Cover: a Conference Abstract}
\author{Mara Quill}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
Over one summer we excluded grazing snails from six of twelve pools with mesh
cages. Algal cover in the caged pools rose from 18\% to 64\%, while open pools
stayed near 20\%. The effect was strongest in the warmest pools (see
\tempdiff).
